A||||13||Songman||Opinions on door windows||||1||
Z||000000||Songman||08-04-2001||01:38 PM||||My T-top threw a belt the other night when my girlfriend was driving it so I went and picked her up and brought her home. It was about 11:30 at night so I waited till the next morning to call a wrecker. Of course, when we got there to pick up my car we found out that some losers must have wanted to check out what was inside my locked car so they knocked the windows out of it...<P>My question is... Should I take the windows out of my 84 parts car and put in my 88 doors? Or should I just put the entire door on and change the outside panels?<P>I am taking the interior parts from the 84 and putting in the 88 anyway, so I thought it may be simpler just to leave the doors intact, or do I have to take them apart anyway to change the exterior parts? I just have a fear of trying to adjust a window in a door.. <P>Thanks.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Raydar||08-04-2001||03:31 PM||||Sorry about the losers. Some people should be sterilized. With a rusty tin can.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>Not the voice of experience, but I've heard the 84 doors are different than the later years. Think they changed in mid-year 85. Dew wipes are not available for the older doors. Seems like the entire door structure is different. i.e., later skins won't work on 84 doors.<BR>Maybe someone else can add...<BR><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||DecadenceR||08-04-2001||04:40 PM||||I don't know about other people, but I used 86 skins on my 84 door. They matched up fine.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/SigPic.jpg">  <BR>AIM - DecadenceR<BR>"For though I cannot fly, I'm not content to crawl..."||||reg||1
Z||000003||Songman||08-04-2001||05:02 PM||||I'm just looking for a temporary fix anyway... I'll add doors with power windows and mirrors as soon as I can afford them... and Australian door skins too!<P>The T-top was completely missing dew wipes anyway. I may just try to bolt the 84 doors on for the time being and see..<P>Thanks guys!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||JohnF||08-04-2001||05:13 PM||||You can change doors but you cannot put '84 skins on '88 frames!  I've been there - tried that! '84 has an upper lip that no other model has.||||reg||12
Z||000005||Songman||08-04-2001||07:22 PM||||But can I put 88 skins on 84 frames? My T-top is an 88 and the parts car is an 84...<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A><p>[This message has been edited by Songman (edited 08-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||JohnF||08-04-2001||08:13 PM||||Let me see if I can remember.  Door skins for any year will fit on any door frame.  Any door frame will fit any door opening.  '84 door skins will not fit any other year door frame but any other door skin will fit any years' door frame. <P>Did I get that right?<P>As an aside, I have an excellent '84 door skin for shipping costs only.  ANYONE - let me know where to send it!<BR>&lt;p&gt;[img] <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1578096&a=12001112&p=52209011&Sequence=0[/img]" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1578096&a=12001112&p=52209011&Sequence=0[/img]</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Songman||08-04-2001||08:40 PM||||Thanks John... that will help me out for my temp fix... then I'll just have to find my good power-equipped doors for the real build-up later....<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||6
Z||000008||Max The Chainsaw||08-05-2001||12:53 AM||||You could just swap the glass from the 84 into the 88 door. Last one I took out took me about 15 minutes to get out.<P>Just remove the inner panel and inner dew wipe, loosen the inner glass rub pads. Lower or raise the window to gain access to the rivets. There are 4 rivets to remove, 2 on the metal track at the bottom center of the glass and 1 in the round plastic stops at each end. Just drive the pin out of the center of the rivets with a punch and drill them out with a 1/4 inch drill.<P>Then you can lift the glass up out of the door. You have to work it around to get the plugs at the ends past the door, but they will come out. <P>When going back together, just use 1/4 X 1" bolts and nuts in place of the rivets.<P>Good luck with whichever method you use.<P>Greg<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Max The Chainsaw (edited 08-05-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||Songman||08-05-2001||02:30 AM||||Thanks Greg... I gotta get my parts car brought home before I can even look at it to decide what I will do! hehe<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000010||rogergarrison||08-05-2001||09:57 AM||||just change the glasses to avoid any aggravation. My rule is never leave a car on the side of the road ever. I had one a long time ago stripped of rad, bat, alt, wheels. Ill even sleep in it broke down if I have too. Any wrecker charge is worth saving possible damage and most insurance will reimburse you for tows anyway. If you dont have it on your policy-have towing added. Its only $4.00 year with State Farm.||||reg||1
Z||000011||DecadenceR||08-05-2001||12:23 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by JohnF:<BR><B>Let me see if I can remember.  Door skins for any year will fit on any door frame.  Any door frame will fit any door opening.  '84 door skins will not fit any other year door frame but any other door skin will fit any years' door frame. <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Not to start an argument, but when i did the door skin on my car, I took an 86 and an 84 and switched them, and they were exactly the sme except for the aero panel on the one. I even put the 84 onto the 86 so they could take it out of here in once piece, and it installed fine. I do not know about the 88s though.||||reg||1
Z||000012||fiero56||08-05-2001||03:31 PM||||I'm not a fan of swapping door frames, as I've stated in other threads.<P>Songman: I've got a pair of door glass in fair/good condition. Driver glass has typical dew-wipe scratching, and passenger side has very light scratching. I looked into shipping them once, and I remember the price was very high, so I still have them. If you or anyone else wants them, come take them off my hands(for free <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">) before I finally put them in the dumpster.||||reg||1
Z||000013||Songman||08-05-2001||06:19 PM||||I appreciate that offer.. and if I had needed them when I was on my way to PA a couple of weeks ago I would have picked them up for sure. I guess I'll just go ahead and take the one out of the parts car for now...<P>The mechanism of adjusting door glass has always been a mystery. That is why I was looking for other options..<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
